+# Tasks
+
+## 1. Repositories
+
+- [x] 1.1 Add `OrderRepository.applyCoupon(id, couponCode, discountCents, finalAmountCents)` that updates the order row; verify with `npm run build` (type check passes).
+- [x] 1.2 Add `CouponRepository.recordRedemption(orderId, couponCode, discountCents, createdAt)` that inserts into `coupon_redemptions` and increments `used_count`; verify with `npm run build`.
+
+## 2. Order service
+
+- [x] 2.1 Give `OrderService` a `CouponRepository` dependency and update the wiring in `src/app.ts`; verify with `npm run build`.
+- [x] 2.2 Implement `OrderService.applyCoupon(id, couponCode)` validation: missing/non-string code → `INVALID_REQUEST`, unknown coupon → `COUPON_NOT_FOUND`, non-`ACTIVE` → `COUPON_NOT_ACTIVE`, past `validUntil` → `COUPON_EXPIRED`, before `validFrom` → `COUPON_NOT_STARTED`, `amountCents < minAmountCents` → `COUPON_MIN_AMOUNT_NOT_MET` (all HTTP 400); verify with the apply-coupon tests.
+- [x] 2.3 Compute the discount (`FIXED`: `min(value, amountCents)`; `PERCENT`: `floor(amountCents * value / 100)` capped by `maxDiscountCents`, clamped to `amountCents`) and persist the order update plus redemption in one transaction; verify with the apply-coupon tests.
+
+## 3. HTTP route
+
+- [x] 3.1 Register `POST /orders/:id/apply-coupon` (parse id, read `body.couponCode`) returning HTTP 200 with the updated order; verify with an in-process `app.request` test.
+
+## 4. Verification
+
+- [x] 4.1 Add focused vitest cases in `tests/apply-coupon.test.ts` covering a valid `FIXED` coupon, a valid `PERCENT` coupon, an unknown coupon, a disabled coupon, an expired coupon, and an order under `minAmountCents`, then run `npm test` and confirm the suite passes.
+- [x] 4.2 Run `npm run build` and confirm the whole project type checks.
+
+## Workflow follow-up
+
+- Archive the change once review/verification requirements are satisfied.
